<title>INDIA: India's SEBI to meet for stock lend, short sales.</title>
<headline>India's SEBI to meet for stock lend, short sales.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Market regulator the Securities and Exchange Board of India (SEBI) is due to hold a board meeting on Thursday to discuss, among other issues, a new takeover code, a SEBI official told Reuters on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The meeting -- scheduled for Thursday morning in Bombay -- will also discuss a stock lending scheme, an amendment in the country's share depository act and a report on short sales, the official said.</p>
<p>She did not give any further details.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
